// What the game's own data calls things: goods, buildings, terrain, trades, faiths,
// peoples, decisions, the modifiers they leave behind, what one country remembers about
// another, the events and the fleets.
//
// Kept apart from the interface's own strings for the same reason the country names are:
// it is a different job. Somebody translating a menu and somebody checking three hundred
// ethnonyms are rarely the same person and never in the same sitting.
//
// The key is the English text exactly as the data file writes it. A mod that adds a good,
// a people or an event ships its own rows for it; one that does not reads in whatever the
// mod called it.
